NAME
    qemu-combined-image.sh - build one GPT image with BIOS and two UEFI loaders

SYNOPSIS
    tests/qemu-combined-image.sh --stages DIR --output DIR
                                 [--bios-modules-dir DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    Takes three previously generated build.sh stages from DIR/i386-pc,
    DIR/x86_64-efi and DIR/arm64-efi. Creates exactly one new 2 GiB raw
    disk file at OUTPUT-DIR/m-boot-combined.raw; an existing output is
    never overwritten. The image uses GPT and contains:
       1   EF02   10 MiB        BIOS Boot Partition, no filesystem
       2   EF00   512 MiB       EFI System Partition, FAT32
       3   0700   remainder     exFAT common loader/data

    The ESP has both EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI and EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI.
    The exFAT filesystem has ONE /m/boot/loader/ tree. The installer is
    called once per EFI target and must confirm the existing loader is
    identical before adding a second EFI binary. The i386-pc bootstrap is
    written with grub-bios-setup ONLY to the loop device backed by the
    fresh temporary raw file, after verifying the loop backing path.
    BIOS boot.img and core.img are first copied to a private temporary
    setup directory because grub-bios-setup resolves both filenames
    relative to that directory. The host GRUB module tree is untouched.
    By default the i386-pc boot.img comes from the tracked verified
    prebuilt/m-boot-i386-pc.tar.xz, temporarily extracted alongside the
    test image workspace; the host grub-bios-setup version is checked
    against its recorded GRUB package version. Explicit
    --bios-modules-dir takes precedence; without the archive, a standard
    host module directory remains a fallback.

REQUIREMENTS
    Linux root for loopback, partition formatting and mounting; matching
    three build stages (which may have been prepared on different build
    hosts), host-side grub-bios-setup and i386-pc boot.img (inside the
    prebuilt/m-boot-i386-pc.tar.xz module directory), qemu-img, sgdisk,
    losetup, mkfs.vfat, mkfs.exfat, mount and umount.
    Select a separate output directory. No physical disk pathname is
    accepted, and the resulting raw file is not a physical install.

EXAMPLE
    sudo tests/qemu-combined-image.sh \
      --stages ./combined-stages --output ./combined-results


LIMITATIONS
    This script creates a boot candidate, not a tested boot. Check the
    same raw file under all three QEMU target modes with qemu-run.sh.
    No physical media or existing disk is repartitioned. In case of
    cleanup failure inspect the reported temporary path/loop device.

